`tests/fixtures/kaggriculture_env_reference_v1.npz` plus `.json` manifest: config/reward coefficients, seeds/stride, source/policy hashes, all transition indices, `lengths int64[16,719,2]`, packed active `tokens int64[sum(lengths),12]` plus `program_offsets int64[16*719*2+1]` (reconstruct canonical zero padding on replay), f32 rewards `[16,719,2]`, bool dones same, before/after f64 banks same, before/after i64 econ `[16,719,2,32]`, final metrics and auto-reset seeds. Store only active prefixes, not the >500MiB expanded fully padded token tensor; no per-turn full observations. Limit **8MiB compressed/256MiB expanded**, stream one game, allow_pickle=False, deterministic ZIP order/timestamps. Hash fixture/export/recorder/policy/reference source with SHA-256; validate manifest before load. Reuse `tests/fixtures/kaggriculture/grammar-v4-reference.jsonl.gz` and its `grammar-v4-reference.manifest.json` from G by hash for extra dense codec cases rather than inventing another corpus.

Reference comparison: every f32 reward bit (two-rounding schedule), done bit, bank f64 bit and counters/seed/terminal step **exact**. Python mathematical oracle separately permits at most one f32 ULP where independently evaluated arithmetic rounds differently, with that derivation recorded; never relax recorded-reference equality without Claude review. First-divergence report identifies game/step/seat/action/field.

